# Only assemble arrays created with --homehost=ts41x-debian (the Debian root/data array on
# partition 3, see docs/handleiding.md). QTS's own system arrays (md4, md9, md13, md256, md322)
# carry another homehost and stay untouched, so the QTS fallback stays intact.
# The initramfs uses this file too: without the AUTO +homehost rule a root on md is not found.
AUTO +homehost -all
HOMEHOST ts41x-debian
MAILADDR root
PROGRAM /usr/local/sbin/ts41x-md-led
# Arrays with another homehost can be listed explicitly:
# ARRAY /dev/md1 metadata=1.0 UUID=...
